    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class with `@Test` methods, and the suite is green.\n\nDone. Here's what I changed to satisfy the new `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` customerCode format:\n\n**`AssignCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 the generator now:\n- prepends `CITY3` = upper-cased first three letters of the owner's `city`,\n- keeps `LAST3` = upper-cased first three of `lastName`,\n- makes `NNNN` a **per-city** sequence: `count(existing owners in the same city) + 1`, computed by filtering `findAll()` on `city` (case-insensitive). Since this step runs before `SaveOwner`, the new owner isn't yet counted, so the per-city sequence increments by one per created owner in that city.\n- Result e.g. `SPR-SMI-0007`.\n\n**`AssignMembershipNumber.java`** \u2014 no logic change needed: it concatenates `customerCode` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), so it automatically rebuilds on the new format (e.g. `SPR-SMI-0007-M26`). I updated its javadoc example to match.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` descriptions and examples to the new format.\n\nI verified the column widths fit: `customer_code` is `VARCHAR(20)`/`TEXT` and `membership_number` is `VARCHAR(30)`/`TEXT`, both comfortably accommodating the longer values.\n\nTest suite: `AcceptanceTest.coreCustomerCodeHasCityPrefix` (asserts `[A-Z]{3}-[A-Z]{3}-\\d{4}`) and the full `mvnw test` run are green \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0.",
